menu "Gesture Board Bring-up"

config APP_FLS2_OFFICIAL_BASELINE
    bool "Build the FLS2 official widgets demo with custom-board power/USB only"
    default n
    help
      Selects a separate main file derived from the downloaded OSPTEK IDF6
      LVGL9 example. Keep the gesture application unchanged. Build with the
      separately generated build_fls2_source/sdkconfig and build_fls2_official.

config APP_FLS2_AUTOTEST
    bool "Repeat FLS2 widgets / solid colors / hardware bars after power-on"
    depends on APP_FLS2_OFFICIAL_BASELINE
    default n
    help
      Diagnostic-only loop, approximately 44 seconds per round. USB commands
      LOOP OFF / LOOP ON pause and resume it. No repeated DCS reads, power
      cycling, panel reset, timing changes or automatic damage verdict.

config APP_COLOR_CYCLE_SEC
    int "Seconds per solid color in display self test"
    default 1
    range 1 30

config APP_AUDIO_BEEP
    bool "Play a 1 kHz beep at startup (enables PA)"
    default n

config APP_RADAR_HEXDUMP
    bool "Hex-dump radar UART data"
    default y

config APP_USB_HID_ENABLE
    bool "TinyUSB composite CDC + HID on USB_DM/DP"
    default y
    help
      CDC is the esptool flashing/console channel; HID is the gesture input
      device. The CDC line-state callback reboots the chip into ROM download
      mode so flashing needs no BOOT/EN button.

config APP_SELFTEST_COLORS
    bool "Run solid-color panel self test before LVGL UI"
    default y

config APP_AUDIO_CODEC_INIT
    bool "Program the ES8389 register tables at startup"
    default y
    help
      Writes the official Linux ES8389 init / power-on / unmute sequence.
      Turn this off if you only want bus probing and I2S clocks, e.g. when
      bringing up a new codec revision with an unverified register map.

config APP_USB_DOWNLOAD_ON_LONG_KEY
    bool "Hold power key 3 s to enter USB download mode (ON-only power key when off)"
    default n
    help
      OFF by default: the power key only powers the board on. This build has
      no long-press action and no software power-off.
      Enable only as a host-free fallback to re-enter ROM USB download mode.
      It disconnects USB and reboots the chip; with R13 pulling PWR_HOLD low,
      the reset window can brown out the 3V3 rail.

endmenu
